# SDP fixtures are stored with LF line endings; the tests convert them to CRLF
# themselves (str_replace("\n", "\r\n", ...)). Without this, a Windows checkout with
# autocrlf=true rewrites the fixtures to CRLF, the test then doubles them to "\r\r\n",
# and the parser leaves a trailing "\r" on every value (e.g. setup:actpass). Force LF
# on all platforms so text files are consistent everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
